WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:07.960
The formula for N C R is 'N factorial, divided by R'

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:12.160
factorial times 'N minus R' factorial.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:16.120
What is this? This is the formula for combinations,

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:19.640
but it is not the best way to understand it !

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:25.840
And what is NPR. It's N factorial over 'N minus R' factorial.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:30.920
And this again, is not the best way to understand permutations!

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:35.160
In many books, and videos you would be asked to use this formula,

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.800
if we have to select our things out of N.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:41.480
And we would be asked to use this formula if

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:45.120
we have to arrange our things out of n.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:48.660
I can assure you that if you understand just these two formulae,

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:52.920
you will never really understand permutations and combinations.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.300
There's only one thing you should understand well

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.920
if you wish to master this topic!

00:00:58.040 --> 00:00:59.800
And that's counting !

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.140
If you're able to count well,

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:06.860
then the topic of permutations and combinations will be a walk in the park!

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:11.060
Of course, the counting will not be as simple as counting on your fingers.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:16.700
It's a little more advanced. But don't worry. Counting is easy!

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:20.540
Let's say we have three pens, and two markers.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:25.460
Every item is distinct. No two items are the same.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:28.780
Here's your first question based on counting.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:33.420
In how many ways can we pick any one items from these five?

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:35.680
Understand the question well.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:42.240
In how many ways, can we pick any one item from three pens and two markers?

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:46.080
In how many ways do you think we can do this?

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:54.360
Look at it logically.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:56.460
We can either pick the first pen.

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:02.920
We can call it P1 or the second pen or maybe the third pen.

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:05.000
Or maybe we pick a marker.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.560
The first one or the second one!

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:09.720
We kept saying OR.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:14.060
This or this or this and so on.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:19.300
You can see that there are five ways in which we can pick any one item.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.740
And how do we get a five?

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.280
Three ways in which a pen can be picked.

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:29.980
Plus two ways in which your marker can be picked .Five ways in all.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.100
This is the first rule of counting .

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:33.080
Or !

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:36.420
Or, always means addition.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:39.980
First Pen or the second pen or the third.

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:42.960
Three ways in which a pen can be picked.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:47.140
And similarly, two ways in which your marker can be picked.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.840
Or always means addition.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.460
Now let me ask you another one.

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:57.380
In how many ways can we pick one pen and one marker?

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:00.400
one Pen and one marker!

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.700
Tell me what you think?

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:12.100
We have to pick a pen and a marker.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.840
In how many ways can we pick a pen?

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:18.740
We pick either the first or the second or the third?

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:23.100
Now having picked one pen we need to pick a marker.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:27.400
Maybe after picking the first pen, we pick the first marker.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:31.700
Or May be after picking the first pen, we pick the second marker.

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:37.440
So  one way is p 1 m 1, and another is p 1 m 2.

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:43.720
Or Maybe we pick p 2 and then m 1 or p 2 and m 2 .

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:49.060
In all we can see that there are six ways in which we can pick a pen and a marker.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:51.190
Which are the six ways?

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:52.959
p 1 m 1,

00:03:52.959 --> 00:03:54.790
p 1 m 2,

00:03:54.790 --> 00:04:02.620
p 2 m 1, p 2 m 2, p 3 m 1 and p 3 m 2 .

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:04.920
And how did we get a 6?

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:08.120
3 ways times two ways.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:09.880
Multiplication!

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:15.600
'And' is another rule of counting, it always means multiplication.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:20.520
One pen and one marker 'three ways' multiplied by 'two ways'.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:25.240
One pen or one marker three ways plus two ways.

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:29.860
If you understand these two rules of counting, trust me!

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:36.160
You will be able to solve most problems based on permutations and combinations!

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.300
And this is nothing new!

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:41.979
I am sure you have used this many times in life.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:44.040
Look at this picture!

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:46.380
How many circles do you see?

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:48.980
I doubt you counted each circle.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:51.380
Instead of counting each circle,

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:56.180
you would have noticed that there are six columns and four rows.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:01.560
Because it's AND the number of Circles will be 6 x 4.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:03.620
24 and all.

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:06.500
Don't forget the two basic Rules.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:11.560
AND is multiplication OR is addition.

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.260
The topic of permutations

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:18.360
and combinations is not liked by many students and maybe you as well.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:22.300
So we have covered as many topics and examples as we can.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:27.180
And I can assure you that if you watch all our videos based on this topic,

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.340
you will master the concepts!

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:32.280
So take some time, go through our sessions,

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:36.400
and you will realize how simple this topic is!

